---
import TrustPageLayout from '@/layouts/TrustPageLayout.astro'
---

<TrustPageLayout
  title="About | xtarter"
  description="Production-grade starter templates and conformance tooling for JavaScript and TypeScript projects, maintained by Agustinus Nathaniel."
  eyebrow="xtarter · about"
  heading="Production-grade starters and conformance tooling for JavaScript and TypeScript."
  lede="xtarter is two tools with one idea: start conformant, stay conformant, without anyone having to remember the standard."
>
  <section class="xt-section">
    <h2 class="xt-section-title">Two tools, one standard</h2>
    <p>
      create-xtarter-app scaffolds new projects from five templates, each shipping Biome,
      strict TypeScript, CI workflows, editor settings, and agent skills before your first
      commit.
    </p>
    <p>
      xtarterize brings existing repositories to the same baseline. It detects your stack,
      previews changes with a dry run, and asks for approval before writing, so you keep
      control of your files.
    </p>
    <p>
      Both CLIs are published on npm and documented on this site, with guides for
      configuration, CLI reference, and contributing.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="xt-section">
    <h2 class="xt-section-title">Principles</h2>
    <ul class="xt-checklist">
      <li>Idempotent by contract: running a task twice leaves the repo unchanged.</li>
      <li>Conformance over convenience: generated configs stay strict.</li>
      <li>Composition over coupling: no task assumes another has already run.</li>
      <li>Prefer the ecosystem: existing tools first, custom machinery only when nothing fits.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="xt-section">
    <h2 class="xt-section-title">Maintainer and community</h2>
    <p>
      xtarter is maintained by{' '}
      <a class="xt-link" href="https://agustinusnathaniel.com/" rel="noopener noreferrer"
        >Agustinus Nathaniel</a
      >. Development happens in the open on GitHub:{' '}
      <a
        class="xt-link"
        href="https://github.com/agustinusnathaniel/xtarterize"
        rel="noopener noreferrer">agustinusnathaniel/xtarterize</a
      >.
    </p>
    <p>
      Contributions are welcome. Meet the people behind the project on the
      <a class="xt-link" href="/xtarterize/contributing/contributors/">contributors page</a>,
      or read the repository's contribution guides.
    </p>
  </section>
</TrustPageLayout>
